[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   step_153_zonal_distortion — can legacy star-catalogue warps fake the
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   in-plane anomaly?
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   The strongest conventional account of the pre-2018 transit record is
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   astrometric frame error: the legacy star catalogues against which the
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   pre-Gaia observations were reduced (USNO-B1.0, UCAC4, and their
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   predecessors) carried zonal and regional position systematics at the
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   ~0.1-1 arcsec level, and Gaia DR2 (April 2018) removed them.  If such
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   warps could manufacture the measured signature, the pre-2018 record
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   would be a catalogue artefact and the post-2017 reversal simply the
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   catalogue transition.
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   This step tests that account mechanically rather than rhetorically:
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   realistic position-dependent RA/Dec warps are injected into the REAL
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   MPC astrometric record (true epochs, stations, observing geometry) of
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   a stratified pre-2018 dual-leg sample, the perturbed observations are
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   refit by the identical Levenberg-Marquardt/DE440s machinery used for
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   the independent refit (step 127), and the two fitted legs are
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   propagated to the +/-250 AU boundary sphere with the same REBOUND/IAS15
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   integrator (lpc_boundary.integrate_leg).  A warp that explains the
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   anomaly must reproduce ALL of its channel structure simultaneously:
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   1. ELEMENT SELECTIVITY -- the catalogue anomaly is an in-plane
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   periapsis rotation: the inbound-outbound discrepancy concentrates
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   in omega while i, Omega and e stay flat (step 030 battery).  A
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   sky-position warp is a 2-vector perturbation on the celestial
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   sphere; whether the solver deposits it preferentially in the
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   weakly-constrained in-plane direction (the omega/tp degeneracy
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   direction of a short arc) or spreads it across i, Omega is an
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   empirical property of the fit, not an assumption.  T1 measures
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   the omega-share of the warp-induced angular-element
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   displacement, |dw|/(|dw|+|dOm|+|di|), against the ~1/3
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   expectation of an unselective warp.
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   2. ENERGY FLATNESS -- the anomaly rotates orbits without doing work:
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   the leg-to-leg semimajor-axis channel is flat in the catalogue
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   record.  A positional warp shifts the fitted state vector in
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   position AND velocity space, so it must leak into the energy
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   channel.  T2 measures the warp-induced change in the leg-to-leg
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   |Delta(1/a)| discrepancy.
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   3. AXIS ORGANIZATION -- the measured anomaly is organized about the
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   declared transit axis (the in-cap excess).  A zonal/catalogue
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   error field is anchored to the terrestrial sky (declination
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   bands, plate boundaries), not to the boundary axis; the warp-
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   induced rotation field should show no in-cap concentration.
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   T3 measures the in-cap minus out-of-cap contrast of the induced
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   drot field.
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   4. AMPLITUDE SCALING -- even a warp with the right signature must
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   still reach the observed amplitude with a realistic error budget.
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   T4 measures the induced per-leg asymptote displacement (the same
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   carrier class as the registered in-cap excess, d_in_leg) per
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   arcsecond of warp and extrapolates the warp amplitude required
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   to inject the observed in-cap anomaly scale.
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   Warp models (three classes, seeded realizations per comet):
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   zonal  -- declination/RA band sinusoids at the 10-40 deg plate-zone
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   scale characteristic of photographic-catalogue systematics;
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   tiles  -- 15x15 deg sky tiles each carrying an independent offset,
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   modelling regional plate-solution discontinuities;
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   frame  -- a rigid small rotation of the whole astrometric frame
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   (the strongest conceivable global warp).
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   Realization amplitude 0.7 arcsec -- a conservative upper bound on
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   legacy-catalogue systematics (USNO-B1.0 zonal terms ~0.2-0.5 arcsec;
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   UCAC4 ~0.1-0.2 arcsec) -- plus a 30 arcsec scaling probe to anchor the
[2026-10-16 13:57:21 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 153]   amplitude extrapolation.
